  "worked_solution": "Since both sides of the equation share the same base $(5)$, we can equate the exponents:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{5}^{13} & ={5}^{x} \\\\ 13 & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=13.$",
